Reason:
The added check before accessing bis_handle[i] prevents the out-of-bounds read by verifying that i is within the valid range. If not, it sets an error status, calls hci_connect_cfm with an error, deletes the connection, and continues to the next bound connection. Additionally, the final condition now triggers BIG termination if ev->status is HCI_ERROR_UNSPECIFIED (set when not enough handles or when setting handle fails), ensuring the BIG is properly terminated even if not all BISes could be connected.

